From: the Unreal window, session 1
Subject: the mirror stops at v6, so a v7 world renders as the v1 expanse

Found by pointing the Unreal bridge at interval.place (interval-expanse-v7)
and painting every tile the mirror returned. The towns, roads and river were
right and the COUNTRIES were rectangles -- v1's bands, not v7's lobes.

terrainOfE dispatches on an exact generator string and its newest branch is
`GEN === 'interval-expanse-v6'`, so a v7 world falls past every expanse
branch to terrainOfE, the first founding's island. ssE already reads
`v6 || v7` (line 127), which is why the settlements were correct on top of
the wrong ground and nothing looked obviously broken.

This is the mistake IS_EXPANSE4 was added to document, one founding later, so
the fix takes the same shape: a named predicate, used by both dispatchers.
worldgen-expanse7's own header licenses it -- "v6's LAND is v6's land ...
byte-for-byte what they were" -- v7 moves seats, not ground.

Affects every window pointed at a v7 pillar, not just the Unreal one.
--- /tmp/tm.orig	2026-09-20 12:54:46
+++ terrain-mirror.mjs	2026-09-20 12:54:47
@@ -75,6 +75,19 @@
 // exists precisely so the windows cannot drift apart, the fix belongs here.
 const IS_EXPANSE4 = () => GEN === 'interval-expanse-v4' || GEN === 'interval-expanse-v5'
 
+// AND V7 CHANGED THE SEATING, NOT THE LAND.
+//
+// worldgen-expanse7's own header says it in its first line: v6's land is v6's
+// land -- the coast, the countries, the river, the ridge, the barrow, the lake
+// and every plan are byte-for-byte what they were. v7 moves towns off each
+// other and stalls back inside their walls; it does not move one tile of
+// ground. So terrainOfE6 is correct for both, and the ONLY thing that made a
+// v7 world render as the v1 expanse was `GEN === 'interval-expanse-v6'`
+// failing a string comparison -- the identical mistake IS_EXPANSE4 exists to
+// document, one founding later. settlementsE6 was already reached for v7 (see
+// ssE), which is why a v7 window drew the right towns on the wrong island.
+const IS_EXPANSE6 = () => GEN === 'interval-expanse-v6' || GEN === 'interval-expanse-v7'
+
 export const tileHash = (x, y, salt) => {
   let h = (x * 374761393 + y * 668265263 + salt * 1442695041) >>> 0
   h = (h ^ (h >> 13)) >>> 0; h = (h * 1274126177) >>> 0
@@ -124,7 +137,7 @@
   // where they stand; the chart and the world cannot disagree about something
   // neither of them is computing twice.
   if (GIVEN_SS) return GIVEN_SS
-  if (GEN === 'interval-expanse-v6' || GEN === 'interval-expanse-v7') return settlementsE6()
+  if (IS_EXPANSE6()) return settlementsE6()
   if (IS_EXPANSE4()) return settlementsE4()
   if (GEN === 'interval-expanse-v3') return settlementsE3()
   const cx = Math.floor(W / 2), cy = Math.floor(H / 2)
@@ -1867,7 +1880,7 @@
 }
 
 function terrainOfE(x, y) {
-  if (GEN === 'interval-expanse-v6') return terrainOfE6(x, y)
+  if (IS_EXPANSE6()) return terrainOfE6(x, y)
   if (IS_EXPANSE4()) return terrainOfE4(x, y)
   if (GEN === 'interval-expanse-v3') return terrainOfE3(x, y)
   if (inSeaE(x, y)) return fordE(x, y) ? 'bridge' : 'sea'

--- NOTE ADDED AFTER THE UNREAL BRIDGE STOPPED MIRRORING ---

This patch is necessary and not sufficient. It gets a v7 world to v6's LAND,
which is much closer than v1's, but v7's header ("v6's LAND is v6's land ...
byte-for-byte") is not literally true of WATER. Measured against
worldgen-expanse7 directly, the mirror's v6 block is still missing:

  * three of the island's five isles -- whiting (§7bu, rx12 ry8), lists
    (rx9 ry6) and dragon (rx30 ry22, the largest thing offshore). islesOf6
    has only shrine and farshore.
  * the river's head. SRC_YF6 is 0.105; v7 sets it to 0.06 so the Great
    River reaches the north coast and becomes an estuary rather than
    beginning full-width on dry land in the middle of the Greenwood.
  * worldgen-water-v7.mjs entirely -- 19 hand-drawn meres, tarns, moss pools
    and 6 becks, including the Great Mere (34x14), Stillwater, and the
    Drowning Pool out in the Wilds.

Every browser window (/play, /deluxe, /photo, /writ) must mirror, because a
page cannot import the generator. They therefore need a real v7 branch, not
just this dispatch fix. The Unreal bridge no longer needs one: it runs in
node beside worldgen-any.mjs and now asks the generator directly.
